{
  "title": "44: al-Dokhaan الدخان",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ ‌ ۛ‌ۚ‏(1)\nHAA MEEEM.\nHa. Mim. (H. M.)\nوَالْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ ‌ ۛ‌ۙ‏(2)\nWAL KETAABIL MOBEEN.\nBy the Manifesting Book (Qur’an),\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ فِىْ لَيْلَةٍ مُّبٰرَكَةٍ‌ اِنَّا كُنَّا مُنْذِرِيْنَ‏(3)\nINNAA ANZALNAAHO FEE LAYLATIM MOBAARAKATIN INNAA KUNNAA MUNZEREEN.\nVerily We sent it down on a Blessed Night - verily We have ever been warning –\nفِيْهَا يُفْرَقُ كُلُّ اَمْرٍ حَكِيْمٍۙ‏(4)\nFEEHAA YUFRAQO KULLO AMRIN HAKEEMIN.\nTherein are made distinct all wise affairs,\nاَمْرًا مِّنْ عِنْدِنَا‌ؕ اِنَّا كُنَّا مُرْسِلِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(5)\nAMRAM MIN I’NDENAA, INNAA KUNNAA MURSALEEN.\n(Becoming) a command from unto Us; Verily, We are the senders (of mercy and peace).\nرَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُۙ‏(6)\nRAHMATIM MIR RABBEK, INNAHU HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEMO.\nA mercy from thy Lord; Verily, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing,\nرَبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا‌ۘ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّوْقِنِيْنَ‏(7)\nRABBIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA, IN KUNTUM MOOQENEEN.\nThe Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them two, if ye be sure in faith.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ‌ؕ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(8)\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA YOHYEE WA YOMEET, RABBOKUM WA RABBO AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\nThere is no god but He; He giveth life and causeth death; your Lord and the Lord of your fathers of yore.\nبَلْ هُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ يَّلْعَبُوْنَ‏(9)\nBAL HUM FEE SHAKKINY YAL-A’BOON.\nYet they are sporting in doubt.\nفَارْتَقِبْ يَوْمَ تَاْتِى السَّمَآءُ بِدُخَانٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(10)\nFARTAQIB YAWMA TAATIS SAMAAA-O BE-DOKHAANIM MOBEENIY.\nSo await thou the day when the heaven shall give out a smoke clearly visible,\nيَغْشَى النَّاسَ‌ؕ هٰذَا عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(11)\nYAGHSHAN NAAS, HAAZAA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nEnveloping the people; This will be painful chastisement.\nرَبَّنَا اكْشِفْ عَنَّا الْعَذَابَ اِنَّا مُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(12)\nRABBANAK SHIF A’NNAL A’ZAABA INNAA MOAMENOON.\n(They will say): “O’ our Lord! Remove from us the torment; Verily we are believers!\nاَنّٰى لَهُمُ الذِّكْرٰى وَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(13)\nANNAA LAHOMUZ ZIKRAA WA QAD JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUM MOBEENUN.\nHow shall they be admonished when there came unto them an apostle making (the truth) mani fest,\nثُمَّ تَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ وَقَالُوْا مُعَلَّمٌ مَّجْنُوْنٌ‌ۘ‏(14)\nSUMMA TAWALLAW A’NHO WA QAALOO MO-A’LLAMUM MAJNOON.\n(And yet) turned they their backs unto him and said: “(He is) tutored (by others), a mad man.\nاِنَّا كَاشِفُوا الْعَذَابِ قَلِيْلًا اِنَّكُمْ عَآئِدُوْنَ‌ۘ‏(15)\nINNAA KAASHEFUL A’ZAABE QALEELAN INNAKUM A’AA-EDOON.\nVerily, We will remove the torment a little (but) verily, ye will return (unto evil).\nيَوْمَ نَبْطِشُ الْبَطْشَةَ الْكُبْرٰى‌ۚ اِنَّا مُنْتَقِمُوْنَ‏(16)\nYAWMA NABTESHUL BATSHATAL KUBRAA, INNAA MUNTAQEMOON.\nThat day We shall seize (them) with a great seizure; Verily, We shall retribute (them).\nوَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَ جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ كَرِيْمٌۙ‏(17)\nWA LAQAD FATANNAA QABLAHUM QAWMA FIR-A’WNA WA JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUN KAREEMUN.\nAnd indeed We tried before them the people of Pharaoh, and there came unto them a noble Apostle,\nاَنْ اَدُّوْۤا اِلَىَّ عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(18)\nAN ADDOO ELAYYA E’BAADAL LAAH, INNEE LAKUM RASOOLUN AMEENUNW.\nSaying: “Deliver unto me the servants of God; Verily, I am unto you a trusted apostle,\nوَّاَنْ لَّا تَعْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ‌ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اٰتِيْكُمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(19)\nWA AL LAA TA’LOO A’LAL LAAH, INNEE AATEEKUM BESULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nAnd that exalt ye not yourselves against God; Verily, I come unto you with an authority manifest.\nوَاِنِّىْ عُذْتُ بِرَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ اَنْ تَرْجُمُوْنِ ۚ‏(20)\nWA INNEE U’ZTO BE-RABBEE WA RABBEKUM AN TARJOMOON.\nAnd verily, I take refuge with my Lord and your Lord lest ye stone me (to death);\nوَاِنْ لَّمْ تُؤْمِنُوْا لِىْ فَاعْتَزِلُوْنِ‏(21)\nWA IL LAM TOAMENOO LEE FA’TAZELOON.\nAnd if ye believe not in me, then leave me alone.\nفَدَعَا رَبَّهٗۤ اَنَّ هٰۤؤُلَاۤءِ قَوْمٌ مُّجْرِمُوْنَ‏‏(22)\nFA-DA-A’A RABBAHU ANNA HAA-OLAAA-E QAWMUM MUJREMOON.\n(But they began tormenting him); Then cried he unto his Lord that “these are a people guilty ones\nفَاَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْ لَيْلًا اِنَّكُمْ مُّتَّبَعُوْنَۙ‏(23)\nFA-ASRE BE-E’BAADEE LAYLAN INNAKUM MUTTABA-O’ONA.\n(He was commanded saying): “Then march forth with My servants by night; verily ye will be pursued,\nوَاتْرُكِ الْبَحْرَ رَهْوًا‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ جُنْدٌ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(24)\nWAT-ROKIL BAHRA RAHWAA, INNAHUM JUNDUM MUGHRAQOON.\nAnd leave thou the sea calm; Verily, they are a host that shall be drowned.\nكَمْ تَرَكُوْا مِنْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(25)\nKAM TARAKOO MIN JANNAATINW WA O’OYOONINW.\nHow many have they left, of the gardens and fountains!\nوَّزُرُوْعٍ وَّمَقَامٍ كَرِيْمٍۙ‏(26)\nWA ZOROO-I’NW WA MAQAAMIN KAREEMINW.\nAnd cornfields and dwellings noble!\nوَّنَعْمَةٍ كَانُوْا فِيْهَا فٰكِهِيْنَۙ‏(27)\nWA NA’MATIN KAANOO FEEHAA FAAKEHEENA.\nAnd pleasant things in which they took delight!\nكَذٰلِكَ‌ وَاَوْرَثْنٰهَا قَوْمًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‏(28)\nKAZAALEK, WA AWRASNAAHAA QAWMAN AAKHEREEN.\nSo was it: and We gave them as a heritage unto another people;\nفَمَا بَكَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّمَآءُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَا كَانُوْا مُنْظَرِيْنَ‏(29)\nFAMAA BAKAT A’LAYHEMUS SAMAAA-O WAL ARZO WA MAA KAANOO MUNZAREEN.\nSo wept not on them the heavens and the earth nor were they respited.\nوَلَقَدْ نَجَّيْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ الْمُهِيْنِۙ‏(30)\nWA LAQAD NAJJAYNAA BANEE ISRAAEEELA MENAL A’ZAABIL MOHEENE.\nAnd indeed delivered We the children of Israel from the degrading affliction,\nمِنْ فِرْعَوْنَ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَالِيًا مِّنَ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(31)\nMIN FIR-A’WN, INNAHU KAANA A’ALEYAM MENAL MUSREFEEN.\nFrom Pharaoh: verily he was haughty, (and was one) of the extravagants.\nوَلَقَدِ اخْتَرْنٰهُمْ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(32)\nWA LAQADIKH TARNAAHUM A’LAA I’LMIN A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd indeed We chose them, with prescience, above all creatures (of their times);\nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الْاٰيٰتِ مَا فِيْهِ بَلٰٓؤٌا مُّبِيْنٌ‏(33)\nWA AATAYNAAHUM MENAL AAYAATE MAA FEEHE BALAAUM MOBEEN.\nAnd gave We unto them of the signs wherein was a clear trial.\nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nINNA HAA-OLAAA-E LAYAQOOLOONA.\nVerily these do say,\nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا مَوْتَتُنَا الْاُوْلٰى وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُنْشَرِيْنَ‏(35)\nIN HEYA ILLAA MAWTATONAL OOLAA WA MAA NAHNO BE-MUNSHAREEN.\nThere is naught save our first death and we shall not be raised again.\nفَاْتُوْا بِاٰبَآئِنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(36)\nFAATOO BE-AABAAA-ENAA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThen bring ye (back) our fathers, if ye be truthful.\nاَهُمْ خَيْرٌ اَمْ قَوْمُ تُبَّعٍۙ وَّ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ؕ اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ‌ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(37)\nA HUM KHAYRUN AM QAWMO TUBBA-I’NW, WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM, AHLAKNAAHUM, INNAHUM KAANO MUJREMEEN.\nAre they better or the people of Tubba, and those before them? We destroyed them, for verily they were the guilty ones.\nوَمَا خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا لٰعِبِيْنَ‏(38)\nWA MAA KHALAQNAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA LAA-E’BEEN.\nAnd We created not the heavens and the earth and what is between them both, in sport.\nمَا خَلَقْنٰهُمَاۤ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(39)\nMAA KHALAQNAAHOMAA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nWe created them not but with the truth, but most of them know not.\nاِنَّ يَوْمَ الْفَصْلِ مِيْقَاتُهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(40)\nINNA YAWMAL FASLE MEEQAATOHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nVerily the day of sorting out is the appointed term for all of them,\nيَوْمَ لَا يُغْنِىْ مَوْلًى عَنْ مَّوْلًى شَيْئًا وَّلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَۙ‏(41)\nYAWMA LAA TUGHNEE MAWLAN A’M MAWLAN SHAY-ANW WA LAA HUM YUNSAROONA.\nThe day when a friend shall avail not (his) friend aught, nor shall they be helped,\nاِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(42)\nILLAA MAR RAHEMAL LAAH, INNAHU HOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nSave those on whom God shall have mercy; Verily, He is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful.\nاِنَّ شَجَرَتَ الزَّقُّوْمِۙ‏(43)\nINNA SHAJARATAZ ZAQQOOME.\nVerily, the tree of Zaqqum,\nطَعَامُ الْاَثِيْمِ ۛۚ   ۖ‏(44)\nTA-A’AMUL ASEEM.\nShall be the food of the sinful,\nكَالْمُهْلِ ۛۚ يَغْلِىْ فِى الْبُطُوْنِۙ‏(45)\nKAL-MOHL, YAGHLEE FIL BOTOONE.\nLike the molten brass; shall it boil in (their) bellies,\nكَغَلْىِ الْحَمِيْمِ‏(46)\nKA-GHALYIL HAMEEM.\nLike the boiling of hot water.\nخُذُوْهُ فَاعْتِلُوْهُ اِلٰى سَوَآءِ الْجَحِيْمِ   ۖ‏(47)\nKHOZOOHO FA’TELOOHO ELAA SAWAAA-IL JAHEEM.\n(There will be a cry saying) “Seize ye him, then drag ye him down into the midst of Hell,\nثُمَّ صُبُّوْا فَوْقَ رَاْسِهٖ مِنْ عَذَابِ الْحَمِيْمِؕ‏(48)\nSUMMA SUBBOO FAWQA RAASEHI MIN A’ZAABIL HAMEEM.\nThen pour on his head of the torment of the boiling water.\nذُقْ ۖۚ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْكَرِيْمُ‏(49)\nZUQ, INNAKA ANTAL A’ZEEZUL KAREEM.\n(It will be said again) “Taste thou; Verily thou was forsooth the mighty, the honourable,\nاِنَّ هٰذَا مَا كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(50)\nINNA HAAZAA MAA KUNTUM BEHI TAMTAROON.\nVerily, this is what ye dispute about.\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ مَقَامٍ اَمِيْنٍۙ‏(51)\nINNAL MUTTAQEENA FEE MAQAAMIN AMEENIN.\nVerily, the pious ones will be in a secure place,\nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍ ۙ ۚ‏(52)\nFEE JANNAATINW WA O’YOONINY.\nIn gardens and spring,\nيَّلْبَسُوْنَ مِنْ سُنْدُسٍ وَّاِسْتَبْرَقٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَۚ ۙ‏(53)\nYALBASOONA MIN SUNDOSINW WA ISTABRAQIM MOTAQAABELEENA.\nAttired in fine silk and in rich brocade, (sitting) face to face;\nكَذٰلِكَ وَزَوَّجْنٰهُمْ بِحُوْرٍ عِيْنٍؕ‏(54)\nKAZAALEK, WA ZAWWAJNAAHUM BE-HOORIN E’EN.\nSo shall it be, and We will unite them with fair ones; with wide, lovely eyes.\nيَدْعُوْنَ فِيْهَا بِكُلِّ فَاكِهَةٍ اٰمِنِيْنَۙ‏(55)\nYAD-O’ONA FEEHAA BEKULLE FAAKEHATIN AAMENEENA.\nThey shall call therein for every (kind of) fruit, (being) in security,\nلَا يَذُوْقُوْنَ فِيْهَا الْمَوْتَ اِلَّا الْمَوْتَةَ الْاُوْلٰى‌ ۚ وَوَقٰٮهُمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِۙ‏(56)\nLAA YAZOOQOONA FEEHAL MAWTA ILLAL MAWTATAL OOLAA, WA WAQAAHUM A’ZAABAL JAHEEME.\nThey shall taste not death therein save the first death, and He will save them from the chastisement of the hell,\nفَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(57)\nFAZLAM MIR RABBEK, ZAALEKA HOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nA grace from thy Lord; this is the great achievement.\nفَاِنَّمَا يَسَّرْنٰهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(58)\nFA-INNAMAA YASSARNAAHO BE-LESAANEKA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nSo have We made it (Qur'an) easy in thy tongue that they may be admonished.\nفَارْتَقِبْ اِنَّهُمْ مُّرْتَقِبُوْنَ‏(59)\nFAR-TAQIB INNAHUM MURTAQEBOON.\nTherefore wait thou: Verily, they (too) are waiting.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Dokhaan (The Smoke)\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 59 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if this Surah is recited at night, then seventy thousand angels pray to Allah (s.w.t.) to forgive the sins of the reciter. If recited on Thursday nights, all sins are forgiven and houses are built for the reciter in Jannah. The reward for reciting each letter of this Surah is equal to that of freeing a thousand slaves for seeking the pleasure of Allah (s.w.t.).\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that whoever recites Surah al-Dokhaan in his obligatory prayers will be protected from the torment of the Day of Judgement and will easily be able to give his accounts. His book of deeds will also be given to him in his right hand.\nIf kept in one’s possession, this Surah acts as a protection from the plots of Shaitan. If kept under one’s pillow before sleeping at night, there will be no suffering from nightmares and one will always get good dreams. Keeping this Surah in a place of business makes the trade prosper.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that keeping this Surah as a talisman ensures protection from the authorities and makes people fond of the wearer. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved is a cure for all ailments related to the stomach."
}
